Deactivate Metered connection:
1.	Open Settings
2.	Open Network & internet
3.	Select the connected internet
4.	Deactivate Metered connection

Change DNS:
1. Run on https://dnsspeedtest.online/ multiple times per day, and note down the most dominant servers
2. Open Settings
3. Open Network & internet
4. Select the connected internet
5. Under IP settings, press edit
6. Add the given IP of the provider in the Preferred DNS tab and save

Remove restrictions:
1.	Open View network connections
2.	Right click your connection & select Properties
3.	Select Configure & go on Advanced
4.	Disable Energy-Efficient Ethernet, Green Ethernet, Power Saving Mode
5.	On Speed & Duplex pick the highest
6.	Restart device

Speed up internet:
1.	Press win + R
2.	Type gpedit.msc
3.	Double click on Computer Configuration
4.	Open Administrative Templates
5.	Open Network
6.	Select QOS Packet Scheduler
7.	Double click Limit reservable bandwidth
8.	Select Not Configured
9.	Click apply
10.	Restart PC

Clearing internet cache & resetting errors:
1. Open Command Prompt with Administrator permissions
2. run ipconfig /flushdns
3. run wsreset.exe
4. run netsh winsock reset
5. run netsh int ip reset
6. netsh interface tcp set global autotuninglevel=normal
